  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sierra Leone Shipyard</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dutch shipbuilder Holland Shipyards Group B.V. and local consultancy and logistics company Prima Investment Ltd., have jointly taken over the run-down shipyard in Freetown from the Government of Sierra Leone. They are turning it into a functional yard again named Holland Shipyards Sierra Leone. This yard will target clients in Sierra Leone and neighbouring countries, as the closest shipyards are located at more than 1,000 km away in C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire, Ghana or Senegal.Potential and actual customers are private shipowners and the government for maintenance and repair of for instance ferries, tug boats, passenger and freight ships.Close to 70 staff will be employed at the yard, and will be extensively trained in working with modern tools and equipment in order to meet the high quality standards Holland Shipyards Group Sierra Leone wishes to set.</narrative>
  </description>
